8,"classKey":220,"orderKey":414,"familyKey":3065,"genusKey":10678644,"speciesKey":10704194,"scientificName":"Helodeaster erici (C.N.Forbes) G.L.Nesom","canonicalName":"Helodeaster erici","authorship":"(C.N.Forbes) G.L.Nesom","publishedIn":"Nesom, G. L. (2020). In: Phytoneuron 2020-54: 2.","nameType":"SCIENTIFIC","taxonomicStatus":"ACCEPTED","rank":"SPECIES","origin":"SOURCE","numDescendants":0,"numOccurrences":0,"taxonID":"gbif:10704194","habitats":["TERRESTRIAL"],"nomenclaturalStatus":[],"threatStatuses":[],"descriptions":[],"vernacularNames":[{"vernacularName":"Alakai Swamp island-daisy","language":"eng"}],"synonym":false,"higherClassificationMap":{"6":"Plantae","7707728":"Tracheophyta","220":"Magnoliopsida","414":"Asterales","3065":"Asteraceae","10678644":"Helodeaster"},"class":"Magnoliopsida"},{"key":10704425,"nameKey":36660508,"datasetKey":"d7dddbf4-2cf0-4f39-9b2a-bb099caae36c","constituentKey":"7ddf754f-d193-4cc9-b351-99906754a03b","nubKey":10704425,"parentKey":3137422,"parent":"Leontodon","basionymKey":11089896,"basionym":"Apargia rosanoi Ten.","kingdom":"Plantae","phylum":"Tracheophyta","order":"Asterales","family":"Asteraceae","genus":"Leontodon","species":"Leontodon rosanoi","kingdomKey":6,"phylumKey":7707728,"classKey":220,"orderKey":414,"familyKey":3065,"genusKey":3137422,"speciesKey":10704425,"scientificName":"Leontodon rosanoi (Ten.) DC.","canonicalName":"Leontodon rosanoi","authorship":"(Ten.) DC.","publishedIn":"DC. (1838). In: Prodr. [A. DC.] 7: 104.","nameType":"SCIENTIFIC","taxonomicStatus":"ACCEPTED","rank":"SPECIES","origin":"SOURCE","numDescendants":0,"numOccurrences":0,"taxonID":"gbif:10704425","habitats":[],"nomenclaturalStatus":[],"threatStatuses":[],"descriptions":[{"description":"Leontodon rosanoi is a subcryptic species, very similar to L. hirta (which is often treated under the competing name L. villarsii) (Mariotti Lippi & Garbari 2004; Zidorn 2012). According to Mariotti Lippi & Garbari (2004) L. rosanoi differs from the latter species by (1) a chromosome number of 2n = 22, (2) tetrasymmetric (tetra-zonocolpororate) instead of trisymmetric (tri-zonocolporate) pollen grains (Mariotti Lippi & Garbari 2004: fig. 1–4) and (3) stellate leaf trichomes with an almost smooth instead of verrucose shaft (Mariotti Lippi & Garbari 2004: fig. 9+10), the latter confirmed by Zidorn (2012) to provide a reliable diagnostic feature visible with a magnification of x20 or higher.\\r\\rThe distribution ranges of the two species need further attentation; currently it appears that Leontodon rosanoi occurs along the Apennine chain and the nearby hills, from Liguria to Calabria, while L. hirta is restricted to southern France; overlapping distribution areas may occur in the Cote d'Azur and the Provence in France (Mariotti Lippi & Garbari 2004).\\r\\rThe chromosome number 2n = 22 of Leontodon rosanoi indicates it to be allotetraploid with parental ancestors having 2n = 14 and 2n = 8, respectively. It has therefore likely originated from either a L. hirta-like ancestor (x = 7) and a member of Leontodon sect. Asterothrix (x = 4) (Samuel & al. 2006), but a Hedypnois species (x = 4 or x = 7) as one and a Leontodon species as other ancestor would be also possible in the light of the phylogenetic results (Enke & al. 2012).\\r\\r References \\rEnke N., Gemeinholzer B. & Zidorn C. 2012: Molecular and phytochemical systematics of the subtribe Hypochaeridinae (Asteraceae, Cichorieae). – Org. Divers. Evol. 12: 1–16. // ➪ // \\r\\rMariotti Lippi M. M. & Garbari F. 2004: Leontodon villarsii (Willd.) Loisel. and L. rosani (Ten.) DC. (Asteraceae): nomenclatural, palynological, karyological, and micromorphological aspects. – Pl. Biosystems 138: 165-174. // ➪ // \\r\\rSamuel R., Gutermann W., Stuessy T. F., Ruas C.F., Lack H.-W., Tremetsberger K., Talavera S., Hermanowski B. & Ehrendorfer F. 2006: Molecular phylogenetics reveals Leontodon (Asteraceae, Cichorieae) to be diphyletic. – Amer. J. Bot. 93: 1193-1205.\\r\\rZidorn C. 2012: Leontodon and Scorzoneroides (Asteraceae, Cichorieae) in Italy. – Pl. Biosystems 146, Suppl. 1: 44–51. // ➪ // \\r"},{"description":"The specific epithet commemorates Francesco Antonio Rosano (1779–1843), a jurist, collector in the Basilicata region, botanical author (Rosano 1812) and correspondent of M. Tenore (Pasquale 1894: 267; Ascherson & Graebner 1906–1911: 947 (footnote 5); Settembrino & Strazza 2006), who named several species after him.\\r\\r References \\rAscherson P. F. A & Graebner K. 1906–11: Synopsis der mitteleuropäischen Flora 6(2). – Leipzig: Gebr. Borntraeger\\r\\rPasquale F. 1894: Bibliografia botanica riguardante la flora delle piante vascolari delle provincie \\r\\rmeridionali d'Italia. – Nuovo Giorn. Bot. Ital, ser. 2, 1: 259–284.\\r\\rRosano F. 1812: Saggio della Flora del territorio di Ginosa. – Giornale enciclopedica di Napoli 1 [= Raccolta di viaggi fisico-botanici effettuati del Regno di Napoli dal collaboratori della Flora \\r\\rNapolitata, compilato dal Dottore Michele Tenore]: 415–477.\\r\\rSettembrino G. & Strazza M. 2006: Il giornale economico-letterario della Basilicata. – Pubblicazioni del Consiglio Regionale della Basilicata. // ➪ //"}],"vernacularNames":[],"synonym":false,"higherClassificationMap":{"6":"Plantae","7707728":"Tracheophyta","220":"Magnoliopsida","414":"Asterales","3065":"Asteraceae","3137422":"Leontodon"},"class":"Magnoliopsida"}],"facets":[]}